WEBVTT

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.371
Grid Bot Builder. Grid Bot Blueprint.

00:00:03.371 --> 00:00:08.330
Lesson one. Introduction. Education only.

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:15.823
Not financial advice. This is general

00:00:15.823 --> 00:00:18.243
information and doesn't consider your

00:00:18.243 --> 00:00:20.577
objectives, financial situation or needs.

00:00:20.577 --> 00:00:22.799
Crypto is high risk. You could lose all

00:00:22.799 --> 00:00:28.350
the money you put in. From 19 July

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:40.398
2023 to 16 October 2023, the public daily

00:00:40.398 --> 00:00:45.257
price of bitcoin stayed in a band. The

00:00:45.257 --> 00:00:47.590
lowest daily print was 24930. The highest

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:49.924
was 30331. Ninety days, and the path kept

00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:52.090
returning into the middle. A grid is a

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:54.312
ladder of limit orders built for a path

00:00:54.312 --> 00:00:56.646
that behaves like that. It has nothing to

00:00:56.646 --> 00:00:59.355
do once the path leaves and stays gone.

00:00:59.355 --> 00:01:03.898
By the end you will be able to

00:01:03.898 --> 00:01:05.954
do three things. Name the range, the

00:01:05.954 --> 00:01:08.530
levels, and the stop on this 2023 window.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.067
Point to a day whose close is still

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:15.845
inside the band. Write the stop as the

00:01:15.845 --> 00:01:18.858
day the path leaves 30331 and does not

00:01:18.858 --> 00:01:23.681
return. Think of a ladder leaned on a

00:01:23.681 --> 00:01:25.848
wall. The rungs do not chase you. They

00:01:25.848 --> 00:01:27.903
wait. On the right is the real path,

00:01:27.903 --> 00:01:32.555
not the ladder. The range is the top

00:01:32.555 --> 00:01:38.688
and the bottom you copy from the path,

00:01:38.688 --> 00:01:45.645
before you invent a rung. Here the public

00:01:45.645 --> 00:01:51.553
low is 24930 and the public high is

00:01:51.553 --> 00:01:53.720
30331. Round numbers that ignore those

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:56.109
prints are a different drawing. Seven days

00:01:56.109 --> 00:01:58.498
in this window wicked above 30000. One day

00:01:58.498 --> 00:02:00.831
wicked under 25000. A tidy 25000 to 30000

00:02:00.831 --> 00:02:03.109
box would have been left behind on those

00:02:03.109 --> 00:02:10.401
days. Six equal gaps of about 900 dollars

00:02:10.401 --> 00:02:16.769
fit between those two prints. The rungs

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:35.735
land near 25830, 26730, 27630, 28531, and

00:02:35.735 --> 00:02:39.721
29431, with the ends at 24930 and 30331.

00:02:39.721 --> 00:02:41.554
A limit order sits on a rung. It

00:02:41.554 --> 00:02:43.776
does not run after the price. The daily

00:02:43.776 --> 00:02:45.887
close crossed 27630 ten times in this

00:02:45.887 --> 00:02:48.276
window. That is the path changing sides of

00:02:48.276 --> 00:02:50.387
one rung, not a promise that an order

00:02:50.387 --> 00:02:55.782
would have filled. A fence has a top

00:02:55.782 --> 00:03:03.234
rail and a bottom rail. Inside it, the

00:03:03.234 --> 00:03:05.548
path can wander. The fence on the left

00:03:05.548 --> 00:03:07.659
is the analogy. The band on the right

00:03:07.659 --> 00:03:12.015
is 24930 to 30331. The public path draws

00:03:12.015 --> 00:03:16.563
across this window. We stop on a handful

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.841
of days, not on every print. Every close

00:03:18.841 --> 00:03:20.675
is an example. It is not a fill,

00:03:20.675 --> 00:03:24.823
and it is not a forecast. On 19

00:03:24.823 --> 00:03:32.423
July 2023, the public daily close was

00:03:32.423 --> 00:03:44.290
29914. That day's low was 29794 and the

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.513
high was 30184. The close is inside the

00:03:46.513 --> 00:03:50.956
band of 24930 to 30331. On 8 August

00:03:50.956 --> 00:04:01.129
2023, the public daily close was 29765.

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:10.164
That day's low was 29114 and the high

00:04:10.164 --> 00:04:12.386
was 30177. The close is inside the band

00:04:12.386 --> 00:04:19.156
of 24930 to 30331. On 24 August 2023,

00:04:19.156 --> 00:04:29.488
the public daily close was 26162. That

00:04:29.488 --> 00:04:36.994
day's low was 25915 and the high was

00:04:36.994 --> 00:04:39.161
26555. The close is inside the band of

00:04:39.161 --> 00:04:47.321
24930 to 30331. On 13 September 2023, the

00:04:47.321 --> 00:04:55.936
public daily close was 26228. That day's

00:04:55.936 --> 00:05:04.165
low was 25781 and the high was 26376.

00:05:04.165 --> 00:05:06.276
The close is inside the band of 24930

00:05:06.276 --> 00:05:15.590
to 30331. On 29 September 2023, the public

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:27.248
daily close was 26912. That day's low was

00:05:27.248 --> 00:05:31.217
26722 and the high was 27226. The close

00:05:31.217 --> 00:05:33.329
is inside the band of 24930 to 30331.

00:05:33.329 --> 00:05:42.508
On 16 October 2023, the public daily close

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:55.572
was 28519. That day's low was 27130 and

00:05:55.572 --> 00:05:57.794
the high was 29448. The close is inside

00:05:57.794 --> 00:06:01.246
the band of 24930 to 30331. The stop

00:06:01.246 --> 00:06:08.999
is a sentence about a path, not a

00:06:08.999 --> 00:06:17.933
mood. On 23 October 2023 the public daily

00:06:17.933 --> 00:06:28.093
close was 33086. That is above 30331. By

00:06:28.093 --> 00:06:30.315
14 March 2024 the close was near 71397.

00:06:30.315 --> 00:06:32.704
The summer band was behind it. Write this:

00:06:32.704 --> 00:06:34.981
if the daily close leaves 30331 and does

00:06:34.981 --> 00:06:37.259
not return, the summer idea is finished.

00:06:37.259 --> 00:06:39.481
The chart now draws that leave. The old

00:06:39.481 --> 00:06:41.537
high stays on the screen as the rail

00:06:41.537 --> 00:06:44.592
that was crossed. Worked check, marked

00:06:44.592 --> 00:06:54.675
Example. The window is 19 July 2023 to

00:06:54.675 --> 00:07:00.502
16 October 2023. Low 24930. High 30331.

00:07:00.502 --> 00:07:06.816
Recap, in three lines. The range was the

00:07:06.816 --> 00:07:12.245
real low and the real high, 24930 and

00:07:12.245 --> 00:07:16.443
30331. The levels were six gaps of about

00:07:16.443 --> 00:07:18.731
900, and one rung was crossed ten times.

00:07:18.731 --> 00:07:24.926
The stop was the October leave, when 30331

00:07:24.926 --> 00:07:29.803
stayed behind the path. A chart where the

00:07:29.803 --> 00:07:32.137
price line zig-zags up and down between a

00:07:32.137 --> 00:07:34.081
top line and a bottom line, marked

00:07:34.081 --> 00:07:39.641
Example. A price line crossing a ladder of

00:07:39.641 --> 00:07:41.863
lines, with buy dots on the lower lines

00:07:41.863 --> 00:07:43.807
and sell dots on the higher lines,

00:07:43.807 --> 00:07:46.870
introducing what a grid bot is. Three

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:50.175
cards: a box for the price range, a

00:07:50.175 --> 00:07:52.341
ladder for the levels, and a stop sign

00:07:52.341 --> 00:07:56.208
for when you quit. A shaded band between

00:07:56.208 --> 00:07:58.320
a top line and a bottom line, showing

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:01.807
the price range you pick. A ladder whose

00:08:01.807 --> 00:08:04.029
rungs are price steps, with small order

00:08:04.029 --> 00:08:07.363
tickets waiting on some rungs. Buy orders

00:08:07.363 --> 00:08:11.237
sit on lines below today's price and sell

00:08:11.237 --> 00:08:15.204
orders sit on lines above it. A notebook

00:08:15.204 --> 00:08:17.259
with a written rule and a stop sign:

00:08:17.259 --> 00:08:19.537
decide and write down when you will quit

00:08:19.537 --> 00:08:23.744
before you start. A send button crossed

00:08:23.744 --> 00:08:25.744
out next to a notebook with a tick:

00:08:25.744 --> 00:08:28.805
this lesson never places a real trade. A

00:08:28.805 --> 00:08:32.140
path of eleven stepping stones with a pin

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:34.195
on the first one, showing you are at

00:08:34.195 --> 00:08:37.937
the start of the course. A price line

00:08:37.937 --> 00:08:40.326
that bounces inside a band and then leaves

00:08:40.326 --> 00:08:42.740
through the top and does not come back.

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:46.342
A blank scoreboard crossed out beside a

00:08:46.342 --> 00:08:48.620
notebook: the lesson shows no results or

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:53.242
profit numbers. A notebook sketch of a box

00:08:53.242 --> 00:08:55.576
with eight evenly spaced lines inside it,

00:08:55.576 --> 00:08:59.141
to practise drawing price steps. A paper

00:08:59.141 --> 00:09:01.308
checklist comes first, then the laptop

00:09:01.308 --> 00:09:06.423
screen. A laptop inside a fenced practice

00:09:06.423 --> 00:09:08.534
area: a practice account uses pretend

00:09:08.534 --> 00:09:12.034
money, kept apart from the real market. A

00:09:12.034 --> 00:09:14.779
notebook sketch of a box, a ladder of

00:09:14.779 --> 00:09:16.667
lines and a stop sign, for you to

00:09:16.667 --> 00:09:20.631
point at and name. Three cards showing

00:09:20.631 --> 00:09:22.798
range, levels and stop: draw all three

00:09:22.798 --> 00:09:26.071
before you click anything. Your finished

00:09:26.071 --> 00:09:28.460
notebook with an arrow to the next lesson,

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:32.308
a checklist of what you need. Next lesson:

00:09:32.308 --> 00:09:35.850
What you are going to need. Bring the

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:37.961
page with the band, the gaps, and the

00:09:37.961 --> 00:09:40.239
stop sentence. Leave every figure marked

00:09:40.239 --> 00:09:42.628
Example. No order is sent between lessons.

